erfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T15:30:18-07:00","id":242610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/241240-my-co-pcs-can-t-be-this-psycho?p=242355#post242355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ST told them they will have to hand in their sheets in such case and the characters will become ST characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a boring way to do things, in my opinion. If your character is fervently against their behavior, and they remain hellbend on acting like heinous lunatics, why not enjoy the painful struggle of one character having to make the hard choise between murdering several of his former friends or letting them live and walking away, knowingly unleashing a cell of crazed slashers on the world (A cell which knows about you, and might want to bring you back into the fold, as they decent deeper into madness).<br /> Instead of just writing the entire thing off, let your sole-sane character be pittede against the moral and phycological pitfalls that might arise from thie situation. Whoever comes out alive - your character or your former team of lunatics - gets to continue the choricle.<br /> In the unfortunate event that a party emerges victorious which the ST is venomously opposed to storytelling for, let the characters become ST-controlled villians by that point. Not only will you then have gotten a more organic resolution to your squabble, but no matter what happens, you will have a solid background for the victorious party.<br /> Does your character emerge victorious? Then your character will be weathered by his grueling experience, and his next cell can get the pep-talk of how he killed his last cell because they crossed the line. Better they not share a simmilar fate!<br /> Does your villianous cell-mates emerge victorious? Then they become ST-controlled villians for your next hunter to take care of, and those hunters might uncover the harrowing evidence of how they murdered their former team-mate and sitched him back together via forbidden magics, to construct a quasi-living abomination that now aids their ungodly work!<br /> <br /> You'll either end up with a splendid BG for your hero or a splendid BG for your villians, and all without compromising the characters actions through inorganic behavior brough on by off-game talks.<br /> <br /> Just my 5-cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T10:07:09-07:00","id":245418,"title":"","co